From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topher Campbell <chrs2021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] media: mediatek: add the MT6771 H.264 decoder and encoder

titan_vdec drives the MT6771's video decoder, MT8183's decoder block,
as a V4L2 stateless (request API) H.264 decoder: frame-based, Annex B
start codes, MM21 output in two planes. MT8183's driver hands the
register programming to decoder firmware on the SCP; the MT6771's SCP
runs the sensor hub instead, so this driver programs the block itself:
it parses the first slice header through the decoder's own bitstream
reader, sets up the sequence, picture, reference lists and buffers from
the stateless controls, and the hardware decodes every slice of the
picture on its own.

titan_venc drives its video encoder as a V4L2 stateful H.264 encoder:
NV12 or NV12M in, Baseline out with the SPS and PPS before each IDR
frame, the encoder's own rate control holding the bit rate, and the
STOP command's drain. It programs the block with the register sequence
of MediaTek's library; the rate control runs on the encoder's own
processor from code that firmware file titan/venc_rc.bin carries, taken
from the phone's vendor files and not distributed.
